---
description: Build, test, and manage the Rust toolchain only through cargo and rustup
alwaysApply: true
---

# Cargo and rustup

All Rust work in this repository goes through `cargo` and `rustup`. Do not call compiler or lint binaries, and do not install a toolchain any other way.

Use:

- `cargo build`, `cargo test`, `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy`, `cargo tree`, `cargo metadata`, `cargo fetch`
- `rustup show`, `rustup toolchain install`, `rustup component add`, `rustup target add`, `rustup run`

Do not use:

- `rustc`, `rustfmt`, `cargo-fmt`, `clippy-driver`, or a path under `~/.rustup/toolchains/.../bin`
- `RUSTC`, `CARGO_BUILD_RUSTC`, or a toolchain tarball
- apt, snap, or a system `rustc` when `rustup` is missing. Stop and say rustup is required.

`rust-toolchain.toml` selects the compiler. `cargo` in this tree must be the rustup proxy so that file takes effect. `ci.sh` calls `cargo` and `rustup` only.

```bash
# good
rustup show
cargo test --locked
cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings
rustup target add aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu
cargo test --locked --target aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu

# bad
rustc src/lib.rs
rustfmt --check crates/
~/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/bin/cargo test
```
